Design for remanufacturing is product design that facilitates any of the step involved in remanufacturing. The objective of the design for remanufacturing (DfRem) is to enhance the remanufacturability of the product. DfRem is not a single task, but there are many factors which have to be considered simultaneously. Depending upon the product specification and the properties the designer has to prioritization to the tasks to improve the product recovery through the remanufacturing. Product features and characteristics of the product always affect the remanufacturability of the product as well as the profitability in the business. There are some technical factors which contribute to develop the methods and tools in the design for remanufacturing for the ease of the process of remanufacturing. When the product is not specifically designed for remanufacturing, it is very difficult and costly to recover items from disassemblies and profitability will depend on that. 
Some of the features that influence the remanufacturing process to have a negative impact on another activity. For example, environmental legislation forcing the manufacturer to reduce waste and recover product material gives the positive impact for designing a product for remanufacturing on other hand bans for some material or contain the product cannot be reintroduced in the market means not to be remanufactured. Some parameters are beyond the designer control like demand, fashion and manufacturers prohibitive activities. Still, there are some characteristics of the product that helps the designer while designing the product for facilitating the remanufacturing. If the product life is too long technology may be upgraded at the end of the product in this case subassemblies of the product can be remanufactured of designed accordingly. Some products have relatively static design and low technology change facilitates the designer to design better ways. Cascading of two life cycle of the product in two different markets of developed and underdeveloped countries are also facilities the remanufacturing. Generally, products are designed for the functionality and cost at the expense of environmental issues is not suitable for the remanufacturing. It is the necessity of the globe to develop the techniques based on the end of life management as many of the products are designed up to date without considering recovery strategy and serious environmental concerns.